Building the Debian packages
============================

Two binary packages from one native source package (`papin`):

  * `papin-cli`     — the terminal client (the binary is `/usr/bin/papin`).
                     No systemd, no root.
  * `papin-gateway` — the server: gateway daemon + chroot wrapper under
                     `/usr/lib/papin/`, the setuid enroll helper at
                     `/usr/local/lib/papin/papin-enroll-helper`
                     (root:root 4755, applied in postinst — dh cannot set
                     setuid at install time), the three systemd units,
                     `/etc/papin/gateway.toml` (conffile; the mutable
                     tokens file lives at `/var/lib/papin/tokens.toml`
                     and is NOT a conffile), tmpfiles for `/run`, docs, and
                     the add-peer / e2e.sh tooling.

Build
-----

Run from `rust/` (the cargo workspace IS the Debian source tree):

    cd rust
    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

or `make -C rust deb`. The .debs land in the repo root (parent of `rust/`).

or, from a clean tree without build-dep checks:

    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b -d

Notes:

  * The Rust build runs `cargo build --release` against the workspace at
    `./` via `override_dh_auto_build`. It honors `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` if
    set (e.g. a tmpfs target dir); otherwise the workspace default
    (`rust/target`) is used. dh-cargo is NOT used — plain cargo keeps the
    build identical to development builds. Crates come from crates.io, so
    the build needs network access (or a prepared cargo cache/vendor setup;
    vendoring is not configured here).
  * `Architecture: amd64` — the packages build host binaries; there is no
    cross-compilation setup.
  * Install with `sudo dpkg -i papin-cli_*.deb papin-gateway_*.deb` from the
    repo root (or via a local apt repo). Remove with
    `sudo apt purge papin-gateway papin-cli` — purge also drops the
    `papin-gateway` system user and `/var/lib/papin-gateway`.
